                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system moving over the southern Tasman Sea extends a ridge over eastern SA until early next week, while a trough lies through the far northwest, before weakening over the weekend. A cold front is forecast to cross the Bight on Monday, extending a trough over western and southern SA.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
